{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "operation": "inbox_now",
  "description": "The item's state key (now) and the words every app shows for it. Go checks that the manager computes expected.now and expected.section (status) from the item; iOS, the web app and Android check that the key and the item's fields give expected.text in each language. An item without now (an older hub) keeps each app's own state words and is not covered here.",
  "follow_by_lang": "When a case has input.follow_by_lang, an app checking language L reads follow.who and follow.next from follow_by_lang[L] (the model writes them in the user's language); Go reads the item as it is.",
  "compose": "waiting: (follow.who ? waiting : waiting_anyone) + (follow.check_at ? look_again : '') + (follow.next ? next : ''). check_due: check_due + (follow.next ? next : ''). failed: handling.error ? failed : failed_plain. Every other key is its own text. Order when several hold: done first (by done_by, and by: muted on the newest done entry), then folded, the suggestion keys, then queued (the agent record says queued and has no session yet, while handling already says looking), then the handling keys (looking, agent_working, waiting, failed), follow_up_ask before check_due, then fyi or needs_you by tier. {reason} is handling.error as it was written (already in words, in the language of its time), never agent.error; without it, failed_plain. A key an app does not know, or no now at all, leaves the app on its own state words.",
  "texts": {
    "confirm_reply": {
      "en": "Waiting for you to confirm a reply",
      "zh-Hans": "等你确认回复",
      "ja": "返信の確認待ち"
    },
